WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.575
The dangers are mostly about
privilege creeping in sideways.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:07.831
A client gains a call nobody listed,
and someone grants a broad role in

3
00:00:07.831 --> 00:00:12.237
production to make the error go away;
the test stops that before release.

4
00:00:12.237 --> 00:00:17.413
One user for everything lets the evidence
reader close findings; the split stops it.

5
00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:21.101
A broad role granted to make
it work is caught as an extra.

6
00:00:21.101 --> 00:00:26.400
Basic authentication outside a developer
instance puts a password in a pipeline.

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.288
A secret in the config file is refused.

8
00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:32.950
And paging is tested, so no
waiting finding is skipped.
